  "analysis": "I'm starting with a fresh terminal. I need to:\n1. Explore the available data files (meteorological/hydrological forcing in /root/bcs/, field observations in /root/field_temp_oxy.csv)\n2. Examine the GLM configuration file (/root/glm3.nml)\n3. Run GLM simulation\n4. Validate the output against observations with RMSE < 2°C\n5. Ensure output is generated at /root/output/output.nc for the period 2009-01-01 to 2015-12-30",
  "plan": "First, I'll explore the directory structure and examine what files are available. I'll check:\n1. The current directory structure\n2. The GLM configuration file\n3. The forcing data in /root/bcs/\n4. The field observation data\n5. Check if GLM executable exists",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /root/\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la /root/bcs/\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -20 /root/field_temp_oxy.csv\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which glm\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find /root -name 'glm*' -type f 2>/dev/null | head -20\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

